{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>So they went down, and all that belonged to them, alive into Sheol.</b> They descended to the lowest chamber of Gehenna, for Gehenna has seven chambers, and Sheol is the lowest chamber; and so it is written (Psalms 9): ״ישובו רשעים לשאולה כל גוים שכחי אלהים״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it as the lowest level of Sheol. And the fact that it says ישובו and not ירדו alludes to the intensity of the suffering, which has no end: after they are consumed by the fire of Gehenna they return and are renewed as at the beginning, so that they may again be food for the fire, and so they alternate forever, for all generations; and this is the sense of ישובו." "<b>And I saw</b> in the Midrash: the order of the world is that Sheol, the seventh chamber, is half fire and half hail, and the wicked leap there from fire to hail and from hail to fire, and the angel of Gehenna drives them like a shepherd who moves his flock from mountain to hill and from hill to mountain, as it is said (Psalms 49:15): ״כצאן לשאול שתו מות ירעם״. End." "<b>And they perished from among the congregation.</b> From here we learn that those who come against the Torah and seek to uproot its foundations have no portion in the World to Come; and this is what it says מתוך הקהל — for the entire congregation of Israel all have a portion in the World to Come, but these lost their portion from amid the congregation of Israel. And so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in chapter חלק: Rabbi Akiva said, ״ותכס עליהם הארץ״ — in this world; ״ויאבדו מתוך הקהל״ — in the World to Come." "<b>And it appears</b> to me that it is for this reason he used the expression הקהל, for it should have said ויאבדו מתוך ישראל; but it is as in the language of the verse (Numbers 19:20): ״ונכרתה הנפש ההיא מתוך הקהל״. And do not wonder and say: why should they be punished and banished from the World to Come, given that they were already punished with a severe punishment and received their sentence in this world? For we find in the case of Achan that Joshua said to him (Joshua 7:25): ״יעכרך ה' ביום הזה״, and our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ביום הזה — you are accursed today, but you are not accursed in the World to Come. These wicked men, however, deepened their corruption more, and were worthy of a harsher punishment, namely the destruction of the body in this world and also the soul in the World to Come. And even though they did not merit to have a portion in the World to Come, which is the world of souls that comes after death, they shall immediately come to the resurrection of the dead, for so our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: לעתיד לבא חוזרים — in the future they return, as it is said (I Samuel 2:6): ״ה' ממית ומחיה מוריד שאול ויעל״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:23.848109241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}